## Step 9: Show the Commit Log in Condensed Form

I viewed the full commit history in a compact, readable format using the terminal.

```bash
# Show a condensed one-line-per-commit log with graph
git log --oneline --graph --all
```

Example output:

```
* a3f1c2d (HEAD -> main, tag: v1.0, origin/main) Resolve merge conflict between main and testbranch
* 8b2e4a1 Modify example.qmd on main to create intentional conflict
* 5d9c7f3 Add new section to example.qmd on testbranch
* 1a4b8e2 Initial commit: add RStudio project and example.qmd
```

**Why:** `--oneline` condenses each commit to a single line showing the hash and message. `--graph` draws a text-based branch graph. `--all` shows commits across all branches.

